<div class="mx-auto">
    <div>
        <h5>Fantasy Challenge Rules</h5>

        <ol>
            <li>
                $20 buy-in. Team must be submitted via Venmo to @@Michael_Page44 or @@MalzM3 by 1/10/2026 at 12:00PM 
            </li>
            <li>
                One entry per person. Any duplicate entries will not be entered. Any teams not paid in full will be removed.
            </li>
            <li>
                Teams must include one player from each of the 14 playoff teams, making a total of 14 players per roster.
                <br />
                Teams must include:
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        2 QBs
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        4 RBs
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        4 WRs
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        2 TEs
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        1 Defense
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        1 Kicker
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </li>      
            <li>
                There is no fantasy draft. Submit any players you'd like via the 'Lineup Viewer.' Note that some teams will consist of the same players.
                <ol type="a">
                    <li>
                        In the event of a tie, regardless of whether the teams are identical or different, winnings will be split evenly
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </li>            
            <li>
                There are NO substitutions. If a player is injured, on a bye, or eliminated, their score for any applicable playoff round is 0.0 FPTS.
            </li>
            <li>
                There are no round multipliers
            </li>
            <li>
                All scoring is entered no later than Tuesday after each playoff round ends. Scores are determined via the DraftKings Fantasy Sports App.
                <ol type="a">
                    <li>
                        This is a standard scoring PPR (Point-Per-Reception) league
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </li>          
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>